  "title": "Force-Placed Insurance Under Regulation X 1024.37: What an AI Servicing Agent Has to Get Right Before the Charge Posts",
  "summary": "Force-placed insurance is one of the most expensive servicing mistakes a mortgage program can make and the noticing rules at 12 CFR 1024.37 are mechanical. The agent design we run to keep the 45-and-30-day clocks, the reasonable-basis standard, the refund duty, and the credit-bureau correction synchronized across the systems that touch the loan.",
